From 85cbfd5f49742dfb2b0ac80fb67fb3abe0275180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:50:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CB1: run the HDR10 AI circuits on desktop OpenGL too

CB1 gated its HDR10 AI circuits, and the Dolby Vision transport and GPU
checks they rely on, to OpenGL ES 3.x. A desktop OpenGL build therefore
refused HDR10 and HLG to Dolby Vision with gpu-processing-unavailable.

Desktop GL compiles the same GLSL ES shaders through
GL_ARB_ES3_compatibility, GL_ARB_ES3_1_compatibility and
GL_ARB_ES3_2_compatibility, so accept a desktop context that has the
matching extension. The Enhanced DV check's GL_EXT_buffer_storage is
GL_ARB_buffer_storage on desktop GL. The OpenGL ES checks are unchanged.
